  "subtitle": "The watch whose whole face is a finger-touch touchscreen you type on — a pocket data bank on the wrist",
  "why_scout_cares": "The museum's only watch where the entire face is a capacitive/graphic touchscreen you finger-type on for text entry and menu navigation. In 1991, that is a genuinely strange, prescient interaction — a wrist-worn personal data bank you tap like a modern phone. Distinct from every existing wearable (Seiko RC-1000 is a keypad, EyeTap mediates vision). Image-verified CC BY-SA 4.0 on Commons.",
